ID   2.7.1.11
DE   6-phosphofructokinase.
AN   phosphofructokinase I.
AN   phosphohexokinase.
CA   beta-D-fructose 6-phosphate + ATP = beta-D-fructose 1,6-bisphosphate +
CA   ADP + H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme from rabbit muscle displays absolute stereoselectivity for
CC       the beta-anomer of D-fructofuranose 6-phosphate.
CC   -!- D-tagatose 6-phosphate and sedoheptulose 7-phosphate can act as
CC       acceptors.
CC   -!- UTP, CTP and ITP can act as donors.
CC   -!- Not identical with EC 2.7.1.105.
DR   Q9M0F9, PFKA1_ARATH;  Q9HGZ1, PFKA1_ASPOR;  Q8A8R5, PFKA1_BACTN;
DR   Q9TZL8, PFKA1_CAEEL;  O94201, PFKA1_CANAX;  Q8XNH2, PFKA1_CLOPE;
DR   Q8FBD0, PFKA_ECOL6 ;  B1IVG3, PFKA_ECOLC ;  P0A796, PFKA_ECOLI ;
DR   Q66GA8, PFKA_YERPS ;  B1JQU4, PFKA_YERPY ;  P06999, PFKB_ECOLI ;
//
ID   2.7.1.31
DE   glycerate 3-kinase.
CA   (R)-glycerate + ATP = (2R)-3-phosphoglycerate + ADP + H(+).
DR   Q2KJF7, GLCTK_BOVIN;  Q08BL7, GLCTK_DANRE;  Q9VQC4, GLCTK_DROME;
DR   Q8IVS8, GLCTK_HUMAN;  Q9BE01, GLCTK_MACFA;  Q8QZY2, GLCTK_MOUSE;
DR   Q0VGK3, GLCTK_RAT  ;  P77364, GLXK2_ECOLI;  Q9XBL1, GLXK_BACC1 ;
//
ID   2.7.1.40
DE   pyruvate kinase.
AN   phosphoenolpyruvate kinase.
AN   phosphoenol transphosphorylase.
CA   pyruvate + ATP = phosphoenolpyruvate + ADP + H(+).
CC   -!- UTP, GTP, CTP, ITP and dATP can also act as donors.
CC   -!- Also phosphorylates hydroxylamine and fluoride in the presence of
CC       CO2.
DR   Q43117, KPYA_RICCO ;  Q40545, KPYA_TOBAC ;  B8BJ39, KPYC1_ORYSI;
DR   Q2RAK2, KPYC1_ORYSJ;  B8BM17, KPYC2_ORYSI;  Q2QXR8, KPYC2_ORYSJ;
DR   Q6FIS9, KPYK1_CANGA;  P0AD62, KPYK1_ECO57;  P0AD61, KPYK1_ECOLI;
DR   P00549, KPYK1_YEAST;  Q6FV12, KPYK2_CANGA;  P21599, KPYK2_ECOLI;
//
ID   2.7.1.165
DE   glycerate 2-kinase.
AN   D-glycerate-2-kinase.
CA   (R)-glycerate + ATP = (2R)-2-phosphoglycerate + ADP + H(+).
CC   -!- A key enzyme in the nonphosphorylative Entner-Doudoroff pathway in
CC       archaea.
CC   -!- In Hyphomicrobium methylovorum GM2 the enzyme is involved in
CC       formaldehyde assaimilation I (serine pathway).
CC   -!- In Escherichia coli the enzyme is involved in
CC       D-glucarate/D-galactarate degradation.
DR   Q6KZ25, GCK_PICTO  ;  O58231, GCK_PYRHO  ;  Q96YZ3, GCK_SULTO  ;
DR   Q9X1S1, GCK_THEMA  ;  P23524, GLXK1_ECOLI;
//
ID   2.7.9.2
DE   pyruvate, water dikinase.
AN   phosphoenolpyruvate synthase.
AN   pyruvate,water dikinase.
CA   pyruvate + ATP + H2O = phosphoenolpyruvate + AMP + phosphate + 2 H(+).
DR   Q9YEC5, PPSA_AERPE ;  O67899, PPSA_AQUAE ;  O29548, PPSA_ARCFU ;
DR   O83026, PPSA_DEIRA ;  P23538, PPSA_ECOLI ;  O54457, PPSA_ENTAG ;
