ID   3.5.1.14
DE   N-acyl-aliphatic-L-amino acid amidohydrolase.
AN   acylase I.
AN   aminoacylase 1.
AN   aminoacylase I.
AN   benzamidase.
AN   dehydropeptidase II.
AN   hippuricase.
AN   histozyme.
AN   N-acyl-L-amino-acid amidohydrolase.
CA   (1) an N-acyl-L-amino acid + H2O = an L-alpha-amino acid + a carboxylate.
CA   (2) an N-acetyl-L-cysteine-S-conjugate + H2O = an S-substituted
CA   L-cysteine + acetate.
CC   -!- The enzyme is found in animals and is involved in the hydrolysis of
CC       N-acylated or N-acetylated amino acids (except L-aspartate).
CC   -!- It acts on mercapturic acids (S-conjugates of N-acetyl-L-cysteine)
CC       and neutral aliphatic N-acyl-alpha-amino acids.
CC   -!- Some bacterial aminoacylases demonstrate substrate specificity of
CC       both EC 3.5.1.14 and EC 3.5.1.114. cf. EC 3.5.1.15 and EC 3.5.1.114.
DR   K9NBS6, AAM_RHOER  ;  Q6AYS7, ACY1A_RAT  ;  Q6PTT0, ACY1B_RAT  ;
DR   Q55DP8, ACY1_DICDI ;  Q03154, ACY1_HUMAN ;  Q99JW2, ACY1_MOUSE ;
//
ID   3.5.1.16
DE   acetylornithine deacetylase.
AN   acetylornithinase.
AN   N-acetylornithinase.
CA   N(2)-acetyl-L-ornithine + H2O = L-ornithine + acetate.
CC   -!- Also hydrolyzes N-acetylmethionine.
DR   Q5E2E4, ARGE_ALIF1 ;  B5FBP7, ARGE_ALIFM ;  B6EMN5, ARGE_ALISL ;
DR   Q9C5C4, ARGE_ARATH ;  B8D8K5, ARGE_BUCA5 ;  P57155, ARGE_BUCAI ;
DR   P23908, ARGE_ECOLI ;  B7NFQ7, ARGE_ECOLU ;  B6I5H3, ARGE_ECOSE ;
//
ID   3.6.1.1
DE   inorganic diphosphatase.
AN   diphosphate phosphohydrolase.
AN   inorganic pyrophosphatase.
AN   pyrophosphate phosphohydrolase.
CA   diphosphate + H2O = 2 phosphate + H(+).
CC   -!- Specificity varies with the source and with the activating metal ion.
CC   -!- The enzyme from some sources may be identical with EC 3.1.3.1 or
CC       EC 3.1.3.9. cf. EC 7.1.3.1.
DR   Q93V56, IPYR1_ARATH;  Q93Y52, IPYR1_CHLRE;  Q889M7, IPYR1_PSESM;
DR   P21216, IPYR2_ARATH;  Q949J1, IPYR2_CHLRE;  Q9H2U2, IPYR2_HUMAN;
DR   Q8FAG0, IPYR_ECOL6 ;  P0A7A9, IPYR_ECOLI ;  Q5B912, IPYR_EMENI ;
//
ID   4.2.1.52
DE   Transferred entry: 4.3.3.7.
//
ID   4.3.3.7
DE   4-hydroxy-tetrahydrodipicolinate synthase.
AN   DHDPS.
AN   dihydrodipicolinate synthetase.
CA   L-aspartate 4-semialdehyde + pyruvate = (2S,4S)-4-hydroxy-2,3,4,5-
CA   tetrahydrodipicolinate + H2O + H(+).
CC   -!- The reaction can be divided into three consecutive steps: Schiff base
CC       formation with pyruvate, the addition of L-aspartate-semialdehyde,
CC       and finally transimination leading to cyclization with simultaneous
CC       dissociation of the product.
CC   -!- The product of the enzyme was initially thought to be (S)-2,3-
CC       dihydrodipicolinate, and the enzyme was classified accordingly as
CC       EC 4.2.1.52.
CC   -!- Later studies of the enzyme from the bacterium Escherichia coli have
CC       suggested that the actual product of the enzyme is (2S,4S)-4-hydroxy-
CC       2,3,4,5-tetrahydrodipicolinate, and thus the enzyme has been
CC       reclassified as 4-hydroxy-tetrahydrodipicolinate synthase.
CC   -!- However, the identity of the product is still controversial, as more
CC       recently it has been suggested that it may be (S)-2,3-
CC       dihydrodipicolinate after all.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.2.1.52.
DR   Q9LZX6, DAPA1_ARATH;  Q97GI9, DAPA1_CLOAB;  Q9KC32, DAPA1_HALH5;
DR   Q9X9W0, DAPA1_STRCO;  P24846, DAPA1_WHEAT;  Q9FVC8, DAPA2_ARATH;
DR   P63943, DAPA_ECOL6 ;  B1IWI1, DAPA_ECOLC ;  P0A6L2, DAPA_ECOLI ;
//
ID   5.3.1.9
DE   glucose-6-phosphate isomerase.
AN   D-glucose-6-phosphate ketol-isomerase.
AN   hexose monophosphate isomerase.
AN   hexosephosphate isomerase.
AN   oxoisomerase.
AN   phosphoglucoisomerase.
AN   phosphoglucose isomerase.
AN   phosphohexoisomerase.
AN   phosphohexomutase.
AN   phosphohexose isomerase.
AN   phosphosaccharomutase.
CA   alpha-D-glucose 6-phosphate = beta-D-fructose 6-phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme from yeast catalyzes the reversible conversion
CC       specifically between the alpha-D-glucose 6-phosphate and beta-D-
CC       fructofuranose 6-phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme also catalyzes the anomerization of both D-hexose
CC       6-phosphates.
DR   Q1QZ19, G6PI1_CHRI1;  Q7P1R4, G6PI1_CHRVO;  P54234, G6PI1_CLAAR;
DR   P54235, G6PI1_CLACO;  P54236, G6PI1_CLAFR;  P34796, G6PI1_CLALE;
DR   P0A6T1, G6PI_ECOLI ;  B7NFW8, G6PI_ECOLU ;  B6I5N7, G6PI_ECOSE ;
//
